# Line endings, settled once.
#
# This repo is written on Windows and almost every file was already LF, but the tools that edit it are
# not agreed about that: a sed pass writes LF and some editors write CRLF, so a one-line change to a
# CRLF file arrives as a diff of the entire file and buries the actual edit. That happened to
# Models.cs and cityboard97.cjs in the fuel-price commit — two real lines inside eight thousand lines
# of noise — which is a poor way to find out.
#
# LF in the repository, whatever the working tree does. Git normalises on the way in.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored Chrome profile under the manual is not ours to reformat. Thousands of files of
# minified extension code and binary blobs, checked in as they came, and normalising them would
# rewrite the lot for no benefit.
docs/manual/chromeprof/** -text

# Genuinely binary, named so nothing is tempted to touch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.ico binary
